 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the administrative code of the city of New York, in relation\nto membership in the New York city teachers' retirement system",
    "basePrintNo": "S6690",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6690-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §13-501, NYC Ad Cd",
    "lawSection": "New York City Administrative Code",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6690\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the administrative code of the city of New York, in\nrelation to membership in the New York city teachers' retirement system\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill is intended to ensure that paraprofessionals are eligible for\nand receive the pension to which they are entitled.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill amends section 13-501(7)(a) of the Administra-\ntive Code of the City of New York to eliminate the requirement that a\nparaprofessional join the New York City Teachers' Retirement System.\n\nSection two of this bill provides that this act shall take effect imme-\ndiately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSome paraprofessionals (teacher aide, educational associate, auxiliary\ntrainer, bilingual professional assistant, family worker, family associ-\nate, and parent program assistant) under the current system neglected to\njoin the retirement system when they began employment and years later\ndiscovered that they had not accumulated an appropriate retirement bene-\nfit. This legislation will treat paraprofessionals like all other educa-\ntors and ensure that they receive a pension commensurate with their\nyears of dedicated service by eliminating the requirement that they file\nan application to become a member of the NYS Teachers Retirements\nSystem, thus making enrollment automatic and mandatory for these para-\nprofessionals.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: S5905A - Vetoed, Veto Memo No. 279\n2018: S5866A - Committed to Rules\n2017: S5866- Advanced 3rd Reading\n2016: S7423 - Referred to Civil Service and Pensions\n2008: S6094-A - Advanced to 3rd Reading\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee bill\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate\n",
